          "content": "167"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.081,
            0.635,
            0.137
          ],
          "content": "7. Suppose you view the tree shown in Fig. 11.19 through a pinhole camera. Sketch the outline of the image of the tree formed in the pinhole camera."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.14,
            0.634,
            0.231
          ],
          "content": "8. Write your name on a piece of paper and hold it in front of a plane mirror such that the paper is parallel to the mirror. Sketch the image. What difference do you notice? Explain the reason for the difference."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.643,
            0.07,
            0.712,
            0.215
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [
            {
              "bbox": [
                0.642,
                0.218,
                0.715,
                0.234
              ],
              "content": "Fig. 11.19"
            }
          ],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_14_image_3.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.235,
            0.726,
            0.272
          ],
          "content": "9. Measure the length of your shadow at 9 AM, 12 PM, and 4 PM with the help of your friend. Write down your observations:"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.179,
            0.276,
            0.726,
            0.296
          ],
          "content": "(i) At which of the given times is your shadow the shortest?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.18,
            0.297,
            0.51,
            0.316
          ],
          "content": "(ii) Why do you think this happens?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.144,
            0.317,
            0.727,
            0.354
          ],
          "content": "10. On the basis of following statements, choose the correct option."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.178,
            0.359,
            0.726,
            0.395
          ],
          "content": "**Statement A**: Image formed by a plane mirror is laterally inverted."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.179,
            0.397,
            0.725,
            0.434
          ],
          "content": "**Statement B**: Images of alphabets T and O appear identical to themselves in a plane mirror."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.187,
            0.436,
            0.448,
            0.453
          ],
          "content": "(i) Both statements are true"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.181,
            0.456,
            0.451,
            0.474
          ],
          "content": "(ii) Both statements are false"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.18,
            0.476,
            0.614,
            0.495
          ],
          "content": "(iii) Statement A is true, but statement B is false"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.18,
            0.496,
            0.616,
            0.515
          ],
          "content": "(iv) Statement A is false, but statement B is true"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.144,
            0.517,
            0.625,
            0.608
          ],
          "content": "11. Suppose you are given a tube of the shape shown in the Fig. 11.20 and two plane mirrors smaller than the diameter of the tube. Can this tube be used to make a periscope? If yes, mark where you will fix the plane mirrors."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.637,
            0.48,
            0.702,
            0.573
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [
            {
              "bbox": [
                0.633,
                0.574,
                0.706,
                0.591
              ],
              "content": "Fig. 11.20"
            }
          ],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_14_image_16.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.144,
            0.611,
            0.727,
            0.684
          ],
          "content": "12. We do not see the shadow on the ground of a bird flying high in the sky. However, the shadow is seen on the ground when the bird swoops near the ground. Think and explain why it is so."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.159,
            0.7,
            0.411,
            0.722
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Exploratory Projects"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.747,
            0.727,
            0.82
          ],
          "content": "Have you ever seen a firefly where you live? If no, ask your elders if fireflies were seen earlier in your region. If yes, find out the reasons for their not being seen anymore. Develop a story about it."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.825,
            0.728,
            0.863
          ],
          "content": "Repeat Activity 11.4, but this time cover the face of the torch with a coloured transparent paper and observe the colour of"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.775,
            0.249,
            0.849,
            0.262
          ],
          "content": "**INNOVATION**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.781,
            0.293,
            0.846,
            0.306
          ],
          "content": "**DISCOVERY**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.774,
            0.382,
            0.851,
            0.395
          ],
          "content": "**EXPLORATION**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.781,
            0.421,
            0.844,
            0.435
          ],
          "content": "**CURIOSITY**"
        },
